---
/**
 * Page-specific callout for docs/vault-layout.md: the one rule of filing, lifted
 * out of thin trailing prose into a single highlighted surface so the eye lands
 * on it. Borderless filled accent surface (no border, no left bar). Scoped CSS,
 * theme-aware via Starlight --sl tokens, no Tailwind on docs pages.
 */
---

<div class="rule">
  <span class="label">the one rule of filing</span>
  <p class="line">
    Filing <strong>adds</strong>, it never removes.
  </p>
  <p class="sub">
    <code>recall</code> searches <code>vault/</code> only, so anything left behind in
    <code>raw/</code> is invisible to it. The note has to carry the source's real
    <strong>payload</strong> in full: tables, lists, IDs, numbers, dates, prices, doses,
    exact wording. The summary goes on top of that, never in place of it.
  </p>
  <p class="test">
    The test before a note is done: could you answer a specific question from the vault
    note alone, without opening the original? If the answer is only in <code>raw/</code>,
    you dropped the knowledge. Put it back.
  </p>
</div>

<style>
  .rule {
    margin: 1.6rem 0 1rem;
    padding: 1.3rem 1.5rem;
    border-radius: 16px;
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--sl-color-text-accent) 13%, var(--sl-color-bg));
  }
  .label {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .line {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--sl-font);
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
  }
  .line strong {
    color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
    font-weight: 700;
  }
  .sub {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
  }
  .test {
    margin: 0.7rem 0 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
  }
  .sub strong {
    color: var(--sl-color-white);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .sub code,
  .test code {
    font-family: var(--sl-font-mono);
    font-size: 0.85em;
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .line {
      font-size: 1.1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
